@startuml API_Design_Architecture

title API Design — Categories + Best Practices

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam rectangle {
    BorderColor #333333
    FontColor #222222
}
skinparam package {
    BorderColor #555555
    FontColor #222222
}

rectangle "API\n(Contract between system\nand client applications)" as API #F4F6F7

package "3 Categories" as Categories #FDFEFE {
    rectangle "Public API\nOpen to all developers\n(requires registration)" as Public #AED6F1
    rectangle "Private/Internal API\nOnly within company" as Private #A9DFBF
    rectangle "Partner API\nOnly for business\nrelationship clients" as Partner #F9E79F
}

API -down-> Categories

package "Best Practices for Good API Design" as Practices #F4F6F7 {

    rectangle "1. Encapsulation\nHide internal implementation" as P1 #D2B4DE

    rectangle "2. Easy to Use\nOne clear way, descriptive\nnames, consistency" as P2 #D2B4DE

    rectangle "3. Idempotency\nSame result no matter\nhow many retries" as P3 #D2B4DE

    rectangle "4. Pagination\nSmall segments via\nsize + offset" as P4 #D2B4DE

    rectangle "5. Asynchronous API\nImmediate response +\ntrack via ID (long tasks)" as P5 #D2B4DE

    rectangle "6. Versioning\nMaintain old + new version\nduring transition" as P6 #D2B4DE
}

Categories -down-> Practices

note right of P3
  Ex: Update address = idempotent
  Ex: Add $100 to balance = NOT idempotent
  Needed because network calls
  can fail/lose messages silently
end note

note right of P5
  Ex: Big reports, video compression,
  large data analysis
end note

@enduml
